cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CodonBench: a four-source decomposition and five-layer control of apparent codon language model advantages"
version: 1.0.0
type: software
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Replication material for the CodonBench manuscript. CodonBench re-examines
  reported advantages of codon language models on synonymous-variant
  classification under leakage-controlled protocols, and separates the apparent
  performance into four sources of predictability: gene identity, exon position,
  sequence background, and a variant-specific component. This repository holds
  the experiment code, the frozen leave-one-gene-out fold definition, and the
  result files underlying every number in the manuscript. Figure-drawing scripts
  are deliberately excluded, because the figures ship with the manuscript.
